## The release's VM flags, read by release/start.
##
## The server runs as one node and uses no Erlang distribution: this file sets
## no -name and no -sname, and ./setup-check refuses one that does.

## Every process keeps its message queue off its heap, whatever ERL_AFLAGS says: the VM's
## abort in major_collection follows move_msgs_to_heap, a step only an on-heap queue takes.
## The paired load run at 150 walkers measured no cost (reductions per move, memory, delay).
+hmqd off_heap

## No Erlang shell: the server is started by a host, not by a person.
-noshell
